RISC3D test kit 35: for the Windows Dev Kit 2023 (15 November 2026)
==================================================================

RISC3D lets RISC OS programs that use Mesa (OpenGL, OpenGL ES) draw with
Linux's graphics driver: on the Dev Kit, the Adreno 690 through Mesa's
freedreno driver. It has only been tried on a Raspberry Pi 4 so far, so
this kit is mostly about finding out what happens on the Dev Kit.

The test image already has everything installed (riscos-risc3d 0.19-1
and Mesa 26.1.6), so there is nothing to install. The programs are the
same as kit 34's; only this file and the devkit script are new.

Steps
-----
 1. Unzip RISC3DTest into HardDisc4 (anywhere will do).
 2. In RiSH's Root shell:
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/devkit
    It writes DevKitLog and DevKit-*.png into the folder.
 3. On the desktop, in a 16 million colour mode, double-click in turn:
      Info     what RISC3D will draw with (writes InfoResults)
      Test     two short runs (writes Results)
      Cube     a spinning cube: please note the frame rate in its title
      Overlay  the same cube shown straight from the GPU, without
               copying (title says why if it can't); frame rate again
      GL       OpenGL 1.x/2.1 (writes GLResults and GLPicture)
      ES       OpenGL ES (writes ESResults and ES pictures)
      GL3      OpenGL 3.x / ES 3.x (writes GL3Results and GL3 pictures)
      Lit      lighting on textures (writes LitResults, LitPicture)
    If one of them fails or hangs, note which, and carry on with the rest.

Please send
-----------
DevKitLog, DevKit-*.png, InfoResults, Results, GLResults, ESResults,
GL3Results, LitResults, LitPicture, the Cube and Overlay frame rates,
and whether anything looked wrong (a screenshot helps).
